 is not a forgery, this is a Christian text 'di epoca postmedievale'",1300,1600,[67,72],{"_":68,"type":69,"ref":70,"region":71},"Drepanum","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462187","Sicilia",{"_":73,"type":74,"ref":75,"region":71},"Trapani","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2522876",[77],[78,79],38.0176,12.53617,{"_":81,"type":82,"subtype":83,"geo":19},"Reportedly found in 1768 during work on the Chiesa di San Pietro, Trapani","found","discovered",[],{"_":86,"type":87,"subtype":88,"geo":19},"None","observed","autopsied",{"_":90,"type":91,"subtype":92,"geo":19},"Lost (manuscript copy only)","not-observed","lost",[],"Sicily",{"_":96,"role":97,"ref":98,"museum":99},"Museo Regionale Agostino Pepoli","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/105",{"slug":100,"type":97,"name":96,"uri":98,"description":101,"location":102},"105","The archaeological collection is housed in one long room that has been subdivided into 4 discrete areas containing 25 cases and a series of open displays. 1 case contains pre- and proto-historic material, 3 are for material from Selinunte, 1 Camarina, 8 Erice, 1 Mozia, 1 Birgi, 1 Lilybaeum, 1 Centuripe, 4 contain material of unknown origin, 1 mixed sites, and then 1 for Punic stamped amphora handles, 1 for Greek and Roman stamped amphora handles, and 1 for Latin epigraphy. In addition there are open displays of material found on the seabed (amphorae, anchor parts, a Roman ram from the Aegadi Islands battle), a large two-sided Latin inscription and a section on Arabic and later Jewish inscriptions",{"settlement":73,"region":73,"country":103,"address":104,"geo":105},"Italy","Via Conte A. Pepoli 180. 91100 - Trapani (TP)",{"lat":106,"lon":107},38.01913,12.541978,[109,112],{"_":110,"type":111},"ms.33","inventory",{"_":113,"type":111},"ms.221",{"_":115,"mainLang":116,"languages":117},"Ancient Greek","grc",[115],{"type":119,"bibl":120},"edition",[121,133,143,153],{"type":122,"n":123,"date":124,"citedRange":125,"ptr":126,"ref":127,"inscrip